generateLPPs -- return all LPP ideals corresponding to a given Hilbert function
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        li=generateLPPs(R,hilb)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
      * hilb, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a Hilbert function as a list
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note PrintIdeals: generateLPPs_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPrintIdeals=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => ..., default value false, print LPP ideals nicely on the screen
  * Outputs:
      * li, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of the form {{powers, LPP
        ideal}, {powers, LPP ideal}, ...}

Description
===========

Given a polynomial ring R and a Hilbert function hilb for R modulo a
homogeneous ideal, generateLPPs generates all the LPP ideals corresponding to
hilb. The power sequences and ideals are returned in a list. If the user sets
the PrintIdeals option to true, the power sequences and ideals are printed on
the screen in a nice format.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/32003[a..c];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : generateLPPs(R,{1,3,4,3,2})                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                          2   2   4                               2   2   5  |
|o2 = {{{2, 2, 4}, ideal (a , b , c , a*b*c)}, {{2, 2, 5}, ideal (a , b , c , |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|               3     4                        2   3   4          2   2 3     |
|     a*b*c, a*c , b*c )}, {{2, 3, 4}, ideal (a , b , c , a*b, a*c , b c )},  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                         2   3   5          2   2 2     4                    |
|     {{2, 3, 5}, ideal (a , b , c , a*b, a*c , b c , b*c )}}                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Same example with the PrintIdeals option set to true:

