isLPP -- determine whether an ideal is an LPP ideal
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        B=isLPP I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in a polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if I is an LPP
        ideal in ring I and false otherwise

Description
===========

Given an ideal I in a polynomial ring R, isLPP checks that I is Artinian and
that the power sequence is weakly increasing. Then isLPP computes bases of R/I
in each degree up through the maximum degree of a minimal generator of I to
determine whether I is an LPP ideal in R.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/32003[a..c];                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isLPP LPP(R,{1,3,4,3,2},{2,2,4})                       |
|                                                            |
|o2 = true                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isLPP ideal(a^3,b^3,c^3,a^2*b,a^2*c,a*b^2*c^2)         |
|                                                            |
|o3 = true                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isLPP ideal(a^3,b^4) --not Artinian since no power of c|
|                                                            |
|o4 = false                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isLPP ideal(a^3,b^4,c^3) --powers not weakly increasing|
|                                                            |
|o5 = false                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isLPP ideal(a^3,b^3,c^3,a^2*b,a*b^2)                   |
|                                                            |
|o6 = false                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

