macaulayRep -- the Macaulay representation of an integer
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h=macaulayRep(a,d)
  * Inputs:
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a nonnegative integer
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a positive integer
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of pairs {i,j} of integers
        such that j <= d for all terms, and a is the sum of the binomial(i,j).

Description
===========

Yields the d-th Macaulay representation of the integer a. Given a positive
integer d, each positive integer a can be uniquely represented as a sum of
binomials binomial(b_d,d) + binomial(b_{d-1},d-1) + ... + binomial(b_1,1),
where b_d > b_{d-1} > ... > b_1 >= 0.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : macaulayRep(100,4)                      |
|                                             |
|o1 = {{8, 4}, {6, 3}, {5, 2}}                |
|                                             |
|o1 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : macaulayRep(10,5)                       |
|                                             |
|o2 = {{6, 5}, {4, 4}, {3, 3}, {2, 2}, {1, 1}}|
|                                             |
|o2 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

